{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1253729-questions-about-pillars-and-affinities","id":1253729,"title":"Questions about pillars and affinities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-12T15:42:09-07:00","id":1253729,"title":"Questions about pillars and affinities","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I finally got my friend to lend me his Mummy core book, and I have a lot of doubts regarding Pillars and Affinities:<br /> <br /> <br /> 1. Page 98 states: &quot;If an Arisen has the maximum number of Soul Affinities of a given Pillar when he loses a dot in that Pillar, he also loses access to a relevant Soul Affinity.&quot;; how does exactly a mummy loses dots in a Pillar? I have seen mechanics for losing Sekhem.<br /> <br /> 2. Related to the previous question, the table for Sekhem shows a column Pillars/Turn, does this mean that Pillar maximum is diminished with Sekhem?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T16:07:47-07:00","id":1253732,"title":"","content":"For the first: Shuankhsen can steal dots from Pillars.<br /> <br /> For the second: Yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T23:31:17-07:00","id":1253816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1253729-questions-about-pillars-and-affinities#post1253729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello,<br /> <br /> I finally got my friend to lend me his Mummy core book, and I have a lot of doubts regarding Pillars and Affinities:<br /> <br /> <br /> 1. Page 98 states: &quot;If an Arisen has the maximum number of Soul Affinities of a given Pillar when he loses a dot in that Pillar, he also loses access to a relevant Soul Affinity.&quot;; how does exactly a mummy loses dots in a Pillar? I have seen mechanics for losing Sekhem.<br /> <br /> 2. Related to the previous question, the table for Sekhem shows a column Pillars/Turn, does this mean that Pillar maximum is diminished with Sekhem?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, with question two, are you asking if your Pillar rating drops as your Sekhem rating does? I'm assuming so because of the &quot;related to the previous question&quot;, and if so the answer is no. The Pillars/Turn column refers to the number of Pillar <i>Points</i> you can spend in a single turn, a rating that does indeed drop with your Sekhem. Your Pillar <i>Dots</i> however are eternal and pass on from descent to descent... baring the aforementioned encounters with Shuankhsen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T06:34:03-07:00","id":1253857,"title":"","content":"Another question, what happens to a Guild Affinity if a Mummy switches guilds? Lost? Replaced by the new guild affinity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T07:32:39-07:00","id":1253877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1253729-questions-about-pillars-and-affinities?p=1253857#post1253857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question, what happens to a Guild Affinity if a Mummy switches guilds? Lost? Replaced by the new guild affinity?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would rule that it is replaced by the new Guild Affinity, but I\u2019d probably make a slight delay if it happened in the middle of a game session. Basically, I\u2019d wait to apply the new one until they were settled into the new guild, but that\u2019s just how I\u2019d handle it. Do what works best for your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T05:24:28-07:00","id":1254743,"title":"","content":"And what about Apotheosis? The woman from Rio that achieved it has a guild Affinity, but has status 0","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T07:13:38-07:00","id":1254764,"title":"","content":"I would assume that was a mistake that slipped through, but I could be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i>